  "foundation/sanskrit": {
   "commands": "FOUNDATION SANSKRIT NOTES - keep to the lesson itself.\n- Cover only the lesson: its introduction, its opening verse and numbered verses\n  (१, २, ३ ...) with their पदच्छेद / अन्वय / अर्थ, one शब्दार्थ table and its\n  teachings. Leave out everything else in the PDF, even though it is printed there:\n  extra or closing verses outside the numbered lesson verses (e.g. a \"गीता-पाठ\"\n  or \"हित-सन्देश\" verse), reference lists and tables (e.g. \"गीता के अठारह अध्याय\"),\n  and grammar drills (e.g. \"विभक्तियों का प्रयोग\"). Leaving these out is not a\n  coverage gap.\n- Exactly ONE \"महत्त्वपूर्ण शब्दार्थ\" table: the words of the lesson's verses that\n  matter most. Never a second word list (\"शब्दार्थ विस्तार\", a repeated\n  \"महत्त्वपूर्ण शब्दार्थ\" or similar).",
